---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How feedme.design handles personal information, including analytics, newsletter sign-ups and email.">
  <PageHead title="Privacy" blurb="What we collect, why, and how to ask us to change or delete it. Last updated 19 November 2026." />
  <div class="prose">
    <h2 style="margin-top: 0">Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      feedme.design is published by Chris Kernaghan, who is responsible for how personal information is handled on this site. You can reach him at <a href="mailto:chris@feedme.design">chris@feedme.design</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Reading the site</h2>
    <p>
      You don't need to give us anything to read feedme.design. The site is hosted by Cloudflare, which processes technical information such as your IP address and browser details when you load a page, in order to deliver the site and keep it secure. Apart from the optional analytics described below, the site doesn't set cookies of its own and doesn't use advertising tools.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      If you accept analytics when the notice appears, we use Google Analytics, loaded through Google Tag Manager, to see which pages are read and how people find us, so we can improve the site. Google sets cookies in your browser and receives information such as your IP address, device and browser details, and the pages you view.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you decline, or ignore the notice, neither Google Tag Manager nor Google Analytics loads and no analytics cookies are set. Our basis for using analytics is your consent. We have set Google Analytics to keep event data for 14 months, and Google may process this information outside the UK, as described in its own privacy information.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can change your choice at any time with the Cookie settings link in the footer. Choosing Decline stops further collection and clears the Google Analytics cookies we can reach from this site.
    </p>

    <h2>The newsletter</h2>
    <p>
      The Subscribe button signs you up to the newsletter of We Are Founders, which is run by the same publisher. We collect your email address, and your name if you give it, and we record that you signed up from feedme.design so we can see where our readers come from. We do this with your consent, and you give it by submitting the form.
    </p>
    <p>
      The sign-up form is provided by Ghost, the publishing platform that We Are Founders runs on, and it only loads when you open the Subscribe window. Its code is delivered through a third-party content network (jsDelivr), which will see your IP address when it loads. Every email carries an unsubscribe link, and we keep your details until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them.
    </p>

    <h2>Emailing us</h2>
    <p>
      If you write to us, we use your email address and what you tell us to reply and to follow up on corrections, data requests or story tips. We don't add you to the newsletter unless you sign up for it.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under UK data protection law you can ask to see the personal information we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, and withdraw your consent at any time. Email <a href="mailto:chris@feedme.design">chris@feedme.design</a> and we'll deal with it promptly. If you're unhappy with how we've handled your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we change how we handle your information, we'll update this page and the date at the top.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
